module

public import Degenne2023Existence.D2023.Corollary4
public import Degenne2023Existence.D2023.Theorem12
public import LMLExplore.Identification.Task.Threshold

/-!
# Theorem 6 of [D23]: positivity has maximal difficulty ratio `K`

In the positivity task, which asks whether some arm has a mean below the threshold `γ`, the
smallest maximal difficulty ratio to the static-proportions difficulty over all algorithm
families is `K`, the number of arms: uniform sampling is optimal for this criterion
(Theorem 5), and no algorithm does better. The task is `LMLExplore`'s minimum threshold task,
restricted to the vectors of means of the exponential families of the arms.

The paper writes `H_{𝒞^{sp}}` for the oracle difficulty of the class of static proportions
algorithms, equal to the static-proportions difficulty by Theorem 1. Its proof of the lower bound
lets the low mean `ℓ` tend to the infimum of the means, which does not give a ratio tending to `1`
in general (erratum E3 of `notes/paper-errata.md`); letting the high mean tend to `γ` does.

The upper bound is the one of Theorem 5 for the static proportions family that recommends whether
some empirical mean is below `γ`. Theorem 5 assumes that the samples lie in the closure of the
means of the families (erratum E2), which the statement of Theorem 6 does not; the rate of this
family needs only the upper bound of the large deviation principle of Theorem 12, at the closed
set of the vectors at which it errs, and the monotonicity of the rate functions on each side of
the means, which brings each such vector back to a limit of alternatives with a smaller rate.

## Main statements

* `Degenne2023Existence.limsup_log_errorProb_le_minThresholdTask`: [D23, proof of Theorem 6], the
  exponent of the probability of error of a static proportions family for positivity.
* `Degenne2023Existence.maxRatio_staticDifficulty_minThresholdTask_le`: [D23, proof of Theorem 6],
  the upper bound `(min_j w_j)⁻¹` on the maximal difficulty ratio of that family.
* `Degenne2023Existence.staticDifficulty_minThresholdTask_le`: [D23, proof of Theorem 6], the bound
  `H^{sp}(λ) ≤ KL(γ, λ_j)⁻¹` at a model with an arm `j` below `γ`.
* `Degenne2023Existence.card_le_maxRatio_minThresholdTask`: [D23, proof of Theorem 6], the lower
  bound `K` on the maximal difficulty ratio of every fixed-budget family.
* `Degenne2023Existence.iInf_maxRatio_minThresholdTask_eq_card`: [D23, Theorem 6].

## References

* [D23] R. Degenne, *On the existence of a complexity in fixed budget bandit identification*,
  COLT 2023, arXiv:2303.09468v2.
-/

@[expose] public section

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology InformationTheory Learning LMLExplore
  LMLExplore.Identification

open scoped ENNReal

namespace Degenne2023Existence

variable {α : Type*} [Fintype α] [Nonempty α] {mα : MeasurableSpace α}
  [MeasurableSingletonClass α]

omit [Nonempty α] in
/-- **The exponent of the probability of error of static proportions for positivity**
[D23, proof of Theorem 6]. Let the arm `a` belong to the exponential family generated by `ρ a`
with the statistic `id`, not almost everywhere constant, and let the threshold `γ` be a mean of
every family. Let `𝒜` be a static proportions family with proportions `w` for the positivity task
on the vectors of means of the families, whose recommendation rule `rec` answers whether some
empirical mean is below `γ`. Then at every admissible model `μ`,
`limsup_T (1 / T) log p_{μ,T}(𝒜) ≤ -inf_{λ ∈ Alt(μ)} ∑ a, w a KL(ν_a(λ), ν_a(μ))`.

The family errs only when the empirical means lie in a closed set `F`: some mean at most `γ` if
all the means of `μ` are above `γ`, all the means at least `γ` otherwise. Every vector of `F` has a
rate at least the one of a vector of means that is a limit of alternatives (move one arm to `γ`,
or the arms below `γ` to `γ`), and the upper bound of the large deviation principle of Theorem 12
applies. Unlike Theorem 1, this needs no assumption on the location of the samples (erratum E2). -/
lemma limsup_log_errorProb_le_minThresholdTask [DecidableEq α] (ν : (α → ℝ) → Kernel α ℝ)
    [∀ μ, IsMarkovKernel (ν μ)] {ρ : α → Measure ℝ} (hρ : ∀ a c, ¬ id =ᵐ[ρ a] fun _ ↦ c)
    (hν : ∀ μ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id →
      ν μ a = (ρ a).expFamily id ((ρ a).natParam id (μ a)))
    {γ : ℝ} (hγ : ∀ a, γ ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id) {rec : (α → ℝ) → Bool}
    (hrec : ∀ x, rec x = true ↔ ∃ a, x a < γ) {𝒜 : ℕ → IdentAlg Unit α ℝ Bool} {w : α → ℝ}
    (h𝒜 : ((minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict
      {μ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}).IsStaticProportions rec 𝒜 w)
    {μ : α → ℝ}
    (hμ : μ ∈ ((minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict {μ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}).M) :
    limsup (fun T : ℕ ↦ ENNReal.log (((minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict
        {μ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}).errorProb 𝒜 μ T) / T) atTop ≤
      -((⨅ μ' ∈ ((minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict
        {μ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}).alternatives μ,
          ((minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict
            {μ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}).cost w μ' μ : ℝ≥0∞) : EReal) := by
  set S := {μ : α → ℝ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}
  set task := (minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict S with htask
  have : Nonempty α := nonempty_of_isProbabilityMeasure ((𝒜 0).alg.policyZero ())
  have hνt : task.ν = ν := by rw [htask, IdentTask.ν_restrict, ν_minThresholdTask]
  have hMt (μ' : α → ℝ) : μ' ∈ task.M ↔ ((∃ a, μ' a < γ) ∨ ∀ a, γ < μ' a) ∧ μ' ∈ S := by
    rw [htask, IdentTask.M_restrict, M_minThresholdTask]
    rfl
  have hμS : μ ∈ S := ((hMt μ).1 hμ).2
  have hμM : (∃ a, μ a < γ) ∨ ∀ a, γ < μ a := ((hMt μ).1 hμ).1
  have hi : task.correct μ = {rec μ} := by
    rw [IdentTask.correct_restrict, correct_minThresholdTask]
    ext i
    simp only [id_eq, Set.mem_ofPred_eq, Set.mem_singleton_iff]
    cases i <;> cases h : rec μ <;> simp [← hrec, h]
  set J : (α → ℝ) → ℝ≥0∞ := fun x ↦ ∑ a, ENNReal.ofReal (w a) * (ρ a).expFamilyRate id (x a) (μ a)
  set L := ⨅ μ' ∈ task.alternatives μ, task.cost w μ' μ
  obtain ⟨hLDP, -⟩ := isLDP_empMean_of_isStaticProportions (task := task) (hνt ▸ hν) h𝒜 hμ hμS
  -- On the vectors of means, the rate function is the cost.
  have hJ (μ' : α → ℝ) (hμ' : μ' ∈ S) : J μ' = task.cost w μ' μ := by
    rw [IdentTask.cost_def]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun a _ ↦ ?_
    rw [hνt, hν μ' a (hμ' a), hν μ a (hμS a), Measure.klDiv_expFamily_natParam (hμ' a) (hμS a),
      Measure.expFamilyRate_eq_ofReal_expFamilyDiv (hμ' a) (hμS a)]
  have hJ_cont : ContinuousOn J S := by
    refine continuousOn_finsetSum _ fun a _ ↦ ?_
    refine (ENNReal.continuous_const_mul ENNReal.ofReal_ne_top).comp_continuousOn ?_
    refine ((Measure.continuousOn_expFamilyRate_left (hρ a) (hμS a)).mono subset_closure).comp
      (continuous_apply a).continuousOn fun x hx ↦ hx a
  -- The rate function is at least `L` at the vectors of means that are limits of alternatives.
  have hJL (y : α → ℝ) (hy : y ∈ S) (hyc : y ∈ closure (task.alternatives μ)) : L ≤ J y := by
    have hsub : task.alternatives μ ⊆ S := fun μ' hμ' ↦ ((hMt μ').1 hμ'.1).2
    have h1 := ((hJ_cont y hy).mono hsub).mem_closure_image hyc
    have h2 : J '' task.alternatives μ ⊆ Set.Ici L := by
      rintro _ ⟨μ', hμ', rfl⟩
      rw [Set.mem_Ici, hJ μ' (hsub hμ')]
      exact iInf₂_le μ' hμ'
    exact closure_minimal h2 isClosed_Ici h1
  have hev : ∀ᶠ t in 𝓝 γ, ∀ b, t ∈ (ρ b).expFamilyMeans id :=
    eventually_all.2 fun b ↦ Measure.expFamilyMeans_mem_nhds (hρ b) (hγ b)
  -- A closed set `F` that contains the empirical means when the rule errs, on which `J ≥ L`.
  obtain ⟨F, hF, hFerr, hFJ⟩ : ∃ F : Set (α → ℝ), IsClosed F ∧
      (∀ x, rec x ∉ task.correct μ → x ∈ F) ∧ ∀ x ∈ F, L ≤ J x := by
    by_cases h : ∃ a, μ a < γ
    · -- The answer is `true`: the rule errs when all the empirical means are at least `γ`.
      have hrμ : rec μ = true := (hrec μ).2 h
      refine ⟨{x | ∀ a, γ ≤ x a}, ?_, fun x hx ↦ ?_, fun x hx ↦ ?_⟩
      · simp only [Set.ofPred_forall]
        exact isClosed_iInter fun a ↦ isClosed_le continuous_const (continuous_apply a)
      · rw [hi, hrμ, Set.mem_singleton_iff, hrec] at hx
        exact fun a ↦ not_lt.1 fun ha ↦ hx ⟨a, ha⟩
      · -- The vector `max μ γ` is a limit of alternatives, and `J` is smaller there.
        have hyS : (fun b ↦ max (μ b) γ) ∈ S := fun b ↦ by
          rcases max_choice (μ b) γ with h | h <;> simp only [h]
          exacts [hμS b, hγ b]
        have hyc : (fun b ↦ max (μ b) γ) ∈ closure (task.alternatives μ) := by
          refine mem_closure_of_tendsto (f := fun t b ↦ max (μ b) t) (b := 𝓝[>] γ) ?_ ?_
          · exact ((continuous_pi fun b ↦ continuous_const.max continuous_id).tendsto γ).mono_left
              nhdsWithin_le_nhds
          · filter_upwards [self_mem_nhdsWithin, nhdsWithin_le_nhds hev] with t ht htm
            rw [task.alternatives_eq_alt hi, hrμ, IdentTask.alt_restrict]
            refine ⟨(mem_alt_minThresholdTask_true_iff ν id).2 fun b ↦
              (Set.mem_Ioi.1 ht).trans_le (le_max_right _ _), fun b ↦ ?_⟩
            rcases max_choice (μ b) t with h | h <;> simp only [h]
            exacts [hμS b, htm b]
        refine (hJL _ hyS hyc).trans (Finset.sum_le_sum fun b _ ↦ ?_)
        gcongr
        dsimp only
        rcases le_total (μ b) γ with hb | hb
        · rw [max_eq_right hb]
          exact Measure.monotoneOn_expFamilyRate_left (hμS b) hb (hb.trans (hx b)) (hx b)
        · rw [max_eq_left hb, Measure.expFamilyRate_self (hμS b)]
          exact zero_le
    · -- The answer is `false`: the rule errs when some empirical mean is below `γ`.
      have hgt : ∀ a, γ < μ a := hμM.resolve_left h
      have hrμ : rec μ = false := by
        rw [← Bool.not_eq_true, hrec]
        exact h
      refine ⟨{x | ∃ a, x a ≤ γ}, ?_, fun x hx ↦ ?_, fun x hx ↦ ?_⟩
      · simp only [Set.ofPred_exists]
        exact isClosed_iUnion_of_finite fun a ↦ isClosed_le (continuous_apply a) continuous_const
      · rw [hi, hrμ, Set.mem_singleton_iff, Bool.not_eq_false, hrec] at hx
        obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hx
        exact ⟨a, ha.le⟩
      · -- The vector `μ` with its arm `a` moved to `γ` is a limit of alternatives, and `J` is
        -- smaller there.
        obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hx
        have hyS : Function.update μ a γ ∈ S := fun b ↦ by
          by_cases hb : b = a
          · subst hb
            simpa using hγ b
          · simpa [Function.update_of_ne hb] using hμS b
        have hyc : Function.update μ a γ ∈ closure (task.alternatives μ) := by
          refine mem_closure_of_tendsto (f := fun t ↦ Function.update μ a t) (b := 𝓝[<] γ) ?_ ?_
          · exact (((continuous_const (y := μ)).update a continuous_id).tendsto γ).mono_left
              nhdsWithin_le_nhds
          · filter_upwards [self_mem_nhdsWithin, nhdsWithin_le_nhds hev] with t ht htm
            rw [task.alternatives_eq_alt hi, hrμ, IdentTask.alt_restrict]
            refine ⟨(mem_alt_minThresholdTask_false_iff ν id).2 ⟨a, by simpa using ht⟩,
              fun b ↦ ?_⟩
            by_cases hb : b = a
            · subst hb
              simpa using htm b
            · simpa [Function.update_of_ne hb] using hμS b
        refine (hJL _ hyS hyc).trans (Finset.sum_le_sum fun b _ ↦ ?_)
        gcongr
        by_cases hb : b = a
        · subst hb
          rw [Function.update_self]
          exact Measure.antitoneOn_expFamilyRate_left (hμS b) (ha.trans (hgt b).le) (hgt b).le ha
        · rw [Function.update_of_ne hb, Measure.expFamilyRate_self (hμS b)]
          exact zero_le
  -- The upper bound of the large deviation principle on `F`.
  have h1 := hLDP.limsup_le_neg_iInf_closure F
  rw [hF.closure_eq] at h1
  refine le_trans ?_ (h1.trans (EReal.neg_le_neg_iff.2
    (EReal.coe_ennreal_le_coe_ennreal_iff.2 (le_iInf₂ hFJ))))
  refine limsup_le_limsup (Eventually.of_forall fun T ↦ ?_)
  refine EReal.div_le_div_right_of_nonneg (by exact_mod_cast T.cast_nonneg)
    (ENNReal.log_monotone ?_)
  rw [h𝒜.errorProb_eq (hi ▸ measurableSet_singleton (rec μ)),
    Measure.map_apply (by fun_prop) hF.measurableSet]
  exact measure_mono fun h hh ↦ hFerr _ hh

omit [Nonempty α] in
/-- **The difficulty ratio of static proportions for positivity** [D23, proof of Theorem 6]. In
the setting of `limsup_log_errorProb_le_minThresholdTask`, the maximal difficulty ratio of the
static proportions family `𝒜` with proportions `w` to the static-proportions difficulty is at most
`(min_j w_j)⁻¹`, as in Theorem 5, without its assumption on the location of the samples.

At every admissible model, the alternatives contain a constant vector, whose costs are finite, so
the maximin value `V` of the static-proportions difficulty is finite; the rate of `𝒜` is at most
the inverse of the cost `L_w` of the alternatives with the allocation `w`, and
`L_w ≥ (min_j w_j) V`. -/
lemma maxRatio_staticDifficulty_minThresholdTask_le [DecidableEq α] (ν : (α → ℝ) → Kernel α ℝ)
    [∀ μ, IsMarkovKernel (ν μ)] {ρ : α → Measure ℝ} (hρ : ∀ a c, ¬ id =ᵐ[ρ a] fun _ ↦ c)
    (hν : ∀ μ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id →
      ν μ a = (ρ a).expFamily id ((ρ a).natParam id (μ a)))
    {γ : ℝ} (hγ : ∀ a, γ ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id) {rec : (α → ℝ) → Bool}
    (hrec : ∀ x, rec x = true ↔ ∃ a, x a < γ) {𝒜 : ℕ → IdentAlg Unit α ℝ Bool} {w : α → ℝ}
    (h𝒜 : ((minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict
      {μ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}).IsStaticProportions rec 𝒜 w) :
    ((minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict {μ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}).maxRatio
        ((minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict
          {μ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}).staticDifficulty 𝒜 ≤
      (⨅ a, ENNReal.ofReal (w a))⁻¹ := by
  set S := {μ : α → ℝ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}
  set task := (minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict S with htask
  have : Nonempty α := nonempty_of_isProbabilityMeasure ((𝒜 0).alg.policyZero ())
  have hνt : task.ν = ν := by rw [htask, IdentTask.ν_restrict, ν_minThresholdTask]
  have hMS (μ' : α → ℝ) (hμ' : μ' ∈ task.M) : μ' ∈ S := by
    rw [htask, IdentTask.M_restrict] at hμ'
    exact hμ'.2
  set m := ⨅ a, ENNReal.ofReal (w a)
  refine iSup₂_le fun μ hμ ↦ ?_
  have hμS : μ ∈ S := hMS μ hμ
  have hi : task.correct μ = {rec μ} := by
    rw [IdentTask.correct_restrict, correct_minThresholdTask]
    ext i
    simp only [id_eq, Set.mem_ofPred_eq, Set.mem_singleton_iff]
    cases i <;> cases h : rec μ <;> simp [← hrec, h]
  -- The alternatives to `μ` are not empty: they contain a constant vector.
  have hev : ∀ᶠ t in 𝓝 γ, ∀ b, t ∈ (ρ b).expFamilyMeans id :=
    eventually_all.2 fun b ↦ Measure.expFamilyMeans_mem_nhds (hρ b) (hγ b)
  obtain ⟨μ₀, hμ₀⟩ : (task.alternatives μ).Nonempty := by
    rw [task.alternatives_eq_alt hi, IdentTask.alt_restrict]
    cases rec μ
    · have hlo : ∀ᶠ t in 𝓝[<] γ, ∀ b, t ∈ (ρ b).expFamilyMeans id := nhdsWithin_le_nhds hev
      obtain ⟨t, htm, ht⟩ := (hlo.and self_mem_nhdsWithin).exists
      exact ⟨fun _ ↦ t, (mem_alt_minThresholdTask_false_iff ν id).2 ⟨Classical.arbitrary α, ht⟩,
        htm⟩
    · have hhi : ∀ᶠ t in 𝓝[>] γ, ∀ b, t ∈ (ρ b).expFamilyMeans id := nhdsWithin_le_nhds hev
      obtain ⟨t, htm, ht⟩ := (hhi.and self_mem_nhdsWithin).exists
      exact ⟨fun _ ↦ t, (mem_alt_minThresholdTask_true_iff ν id).2 fun _ ↦ ht, htm⟩
  have hμ₀S : μ₀ ∈ S := hMS μ₀ hμ₀.1
  set L := ⨅ μ' ∈ task.alternatives μ, task.cost w μ' μ
  set V := ⨆ w' ∈ simplex α, ⨅ μ' ∈ task.alternatives μ, task.cost w' μ' μ
  -- The costs of `μ₀` are bounded, so `V` is finite.
  have hcost_le (w' : α → ℝ) (hw' : w' ∈ simplex α) :
      task.cost w' μ₀ μ ≤ ∑ a, klDiv (task.ν μ₀ a) (task.ν μ a) := by
    rw [IdentTask.cost_def]
    gcongr with a
    calc ENNReal.ofReal (w' a) * klDiv (task.ν μ₀ a) (task.ν μ a)
        ≤ 1 * klDiv (task.ν μ₀ a) (task.ν μ a) := by
          gcongr
          exact ENNReal.ofReal_le_one.2 ((simplex_subset_Icc hw').2 a)
      _ = klDiv (task.ν μ₀ a) (task.ν μ a) := one_mul _
  have hB : ∑ a, klDiv (task.ν μ₀ a) (task.ν μ a) ≠ ∞ := by
    refine ENNReal.sum_ne_top.2 fun a _ ↦ ?_
    rw [hνt, hν μ₀ a (hμ₀S a), hν μ a (hμS a), Measure.klDiv_expFamily_natParam (hμ₀S a) (hμS a)]
    exact ENNReal.ofReal_ne_top
  have hV : V ≠ ∞ := ne_top_of_le_ne_top hB
    (iSup₂_le fun w' hw' ↦ (iInf₂_le μ₀ hμ₀).trans (hcost_le w' hw'))
  -- `L_w ≥ (min_j w_j) L_{w'}` for every `w'` in the simplex.
  have hmV : m * V ≤ L := by
    rw [ENNReal.mul_iSup]
    refine iSup_le fun w' ↦ ?_
    rw [ENNReal.mul_iSup]
    refine iSup_le fun hw' ↦ le_iInf₂ fun μ' hμ' ↦ ?_
    refine (mul_le_mul_right (iInf₂_le μ' hμ') m).trans ?_
    rw [IdentTask.cost_def, IdentTask.cost_def, Finset.mul_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_le_sum fun a _ ↦ ?_
    rw [← mul_assoc]
    refine mul_le_mul_left ?_ _
    calc m * ENNReal.ofReal (w' a) ≤ m * 1 := by
          gcongr
          exact ENNReal.ofReal_le_one.2 ((simplex_subset_Icc hw').2 a)
      _ = m := mul_one m
      _ ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (w a) := iInf_le _ a
  -- The rate of `𝒜` at `μ` is at most `L⁻¹`.
  have hlim : limsup (task.errorRate 𝒜 μ) atTop ≤ L⁻¹ :=
    task.limsup_errorRate_le_inv_of_limsup_le_neg
      (limsup_log_errorProb_le_minThresholdTask ν hρ hν hγ hrec h𝒜 hμ)
  have hratio : task.difficultyRatio task.staticDifficulty 𝒜 μ =
      fun T ↦ task.errorRate 𝒜 μ T * V := by
    ext T
    rw [IdentTask.difficultyRatio, IdentTask.staticDifficulty, div_eq_mul_inv, inv_inv]
  rw [IdentTask.asymptoticRatio, hratio, ENNReal.limsup_mul_const_of_ne_top hV]
  rcases eq_or_ne V 0 with hV0 | hV0
  · rw [hV0, zero_mul]
    exact zero_le
  calc V * limsup (task.errorRate 𝒜 μ) atTop ≤ V * L⁻¹ := by gcongr
    _ ≤ V * (m * V)⁻¹ := by gcongr
    _ = m⁻¹ := by
      rw [ENNReal.mul_inv (Or.inr hV) (Or.inr hV0), mul_comm, mul_assoc,
        ENNReal.inv_mul_cancel hV0 hV, mul_one]

omit [Nonempty α] [MeasurableSingletonClass α] in
/-- **The static-proportions difficulty of a model with an arm below the threshold**
[D23, proof of Theorem 6]. Let the arm `a` belong to the exponential family generated by `ρ a`
with the statistic `id`, and let the threshold `γ` be a mean of every family. For the positivity
task on the vectors of means of the families, every vector of means `λ` with an arm `j` below `γ`
has `H^{sp}(λ) ≤ KL(γ, λ_j)⁻¹`: the alternatives to `λ` have all their means above `γ`, and with
the allocation `δ_j` their cost is `KL(λ'_j, λ_j) ≥ KL(γ, λ_j)`.

The paper states the equality when `j` is the only arm below `γ`; the proof uses only this
inequality, which needs neither that hypothesis nor that the families are not degenerate. -/
lemma staticDifficulty_minThresholdTask_le (ν : (α → ℝ) → Kernel α ℝ)
    [∀ μ, IsMarkovKernel (ν μ)] {ρ : α → Measure ℝ}
    (hν : ∀ μ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id →
      ν μ a = (ρ a).expFamily id ((ρ a).natParam id (μ a)))
    {γ : ℝ} (hγ : ∀ a, γ ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id) {lam : α → ℝ}
    (hlam : ∀ a, lam a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id) {j : α} (hj : lam j < γ) :
    ((minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict
        {μ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}).staticDifficulty lam ≤
      (ENNReal.ofReal ((ρ j).expFamilyDiv id γ (lam j)))⁻¹ := by
  classical
  set S := {μ : α → ℝ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}
  set task := (minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict S with htask
  have hνt : task.ν = ν := by rw [htask, IdentTask.ν_restrict, ν_minThresholdTask]
  have hcorr : task.correct lam = {true} := by
    rw [IdentTask.correct_restrict, correct_minThresholdTask_eq_singleton, id_eq,
      decide_eq_true ⟨j, hj⟩]
  rw [IdentTask.staticDifficulty, ENNReal.inv_le_inv]
  refine le_iSup₂_of_le (Pi.single j 1) (single_mem_simplex j) (le_iInf₂ fun μ' hμ' ↦ ?_)
  rw [task.alternatives_eq_alt hcorr, IdentTask.alt_restrict] at hμ'
  have hgt := (mem_alt_minThresholdTask_true_iff ν id).1 hμ'.1
  have hμ'S : μ' ∈ S := hμ'.2
  rw [IdentTask.cost_def, Finset.sum_eq_single j (fun b _ hb ↦ by simp [hb]) (by simp),
    Pi.single_eq_same, ENNReal.ofReal_one, one_mul]
  rw [hνt, hν μ' j (hμ'S j), hν lam j (hlam j), Measure.klDiv_expFamily_natParam (hμ'S j) (hlam j),
    ← Measure.expFamilyRate_eq_ofReal_expFamilyDiv (hγ j) (hlam j),
    ← Measure.expFamilyRate_eq_ofReal_expFamilyDiv (hμ'S j) (hlam j)]
  exact Measure.monotoneOn_expFamilyRate_left (hlam j) (Set.mem_Ici.2 hj.le)
    (Set.mem_Ici.2 (hj.trans (hgt j)).le) (hgt j).le

omit [Nonempty α] in
/-- **No algorithm beats uniform sampling for positivity** [D23, proof of Theorem 6]. In the
setting of `iInf_maxRatio_minThresholdTask_eq_card`, every fixed-budget algorithm family has
maximal difficulty ratio at least `K` to the static-proportions difficulty.

Let `ℓ < γ < m` be means of every family, `μ` the model with all its means equal to `m`, and
`λ j` the model `μ` with its arm `j` moved to `ℓ`. If the probability of error at `μ` does not tend
to `0`, the ratio at `μ` is infinite. Otherwise Corollary 4, with
`H^{sp}(λ j) ≤ KL(γ, ℓ)⁻¹` (`staticDifficulty_minThresholdTask_le`), bounds the ratio below by
`∑ j, KL_j(γ, ℓ) / KL_j(m, ℓ)`, which tends to `K` as `m` decreases to `γ`. The paper lets `ℓ` tend
to the lower end of the means instead, which does not give `K` in general (erratum E3). -/
lemma card_le_maxRatio_minThresholdTask (ν : (α → ℝ) → Kernel α ℝ)
    [∀ μ, IsMarkovKernel (ν μ)] {ρ : α → Measure ℝ} (hρ : ∀ a c, ¬ id =ᵐ[ρ a] fun _ ↦ c)
    (hν : ∀ μ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id →
      ν μ a = (ρ a).expFamily id ((ρ a).natParam id (μ a)))
    {γ : ℝ} (hγ : ∀ a, γ ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id) {𝒜 : ℕ → IdentAlg Unit α ℝ Bool}
    (h𝒜 : IsFixedBudgetFamily 𝒜) :
    (Fintype.card α : ℝ≥0∞) ≤
      ((minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict {μ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}).maxRatio
        ((minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict
          {μ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}).staticDifficulty 𝒜 := by
  classical
  set S := {μ : α → ℝ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}
  set task := (minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict S with htask
  have hνt : task.ν = ν := by rw [htask, IdentTask.ν_restrict, ν_minThresholdTask]
  have hMt (μ' : α → ℝ) : μ' ∈ task.M ↔ ((∃ a, μ' a < γ) ∨ ∀ a, γ < μ' a) ∧ μ' ∈ S := by
    rw [htask, IdentTask.M_restrict, M_minThresholdTask]
    rfl
  have hev : ∀ᶠ t in 𝓝 γ, ∀ b, t ∈ (ρ b).expFamilyMeans id :=
    eventually_all.2 fun b ↦ Measure.expFamilyMeans_mem_nhds (hρ b) (hγ b)
  -- A low mean `ℓ < γ` of every family.
  have hlo : ∀ᶠ t in 𝓝[<] γ, ∀ b, t ∈ (ρ b).expFamilyMeans id := nhdsWithin_le_nhds hev
  obtain ⟨ℓ, hℓS, hℓ⟩ := (hlo.and self_mem_nhdsWithin).exists
  have hℓ' : ℓ < γ := hℓ
  have hdγ (b : α) : 0 < (ρ b).expFamilyDiv id γ ℓ :=
    Measure.expFamilyDiv_pos (hγ b) (hℓS b) hℓ'.ne'
  -- The lower bound `∑ b, KL_b(γ, ℓ) / KL_b(m, ℓ)` tends to `K` as `m ↓ γ`.
  have hf : Tendsto (fun m ↦ ∑ b, (ρ b).expFamilyDiv id γ ℓ / (ρ b).expFamilyDiv id m ℓ)
      (𝓝[>] γ) (𝓝 (Fintype.card α)) := by
    have hK : (Fintype.card α : ℝ) =
        ∑ b : α, (ρ b).expFamilyDiv id γ ℓ / (ρ b).expFamilyDiv id γ ℓ := by
      simp [div_self (hdγ _).ne']
    rw [hK]
    refine (tendsto_finsetSum _ fun b _ ↦ ?_).mono_left nhdsWithin_le_nhds
    refine tendsto_const_nhds.div ?_ (hdγ b).ne'
    have hmaps : Set.MapsTo (fun x : ℝ ↦ (x, ℓ)) ((ρ b).expFamilyMeans id)
        ((ρ b).expFamilyMeans id ×ˢ (ρ b).expFamilyMeans id) := fun x hx ↦ ⟨hx, hℓS b⟩
    have hc := (Measure.continuousOn_expFamilyDiv (hρ b)).comp
      (Continuous.prodMk_left ℓ).continuousOn hmaps
    exact (hc.continuousAt (Measure.expFamilyMeans_mem_nhds (hρ b) (hγ b))).tendsto
  rw [← ENNReal.ofReal_natCast]
  refine le_of_tendsto (ENNReal.tendsto_ofReal hf) ?_
  filter_upwards [self_mem_nhdsWithin, nhdsWithin_le_nhds hev] with m (hm : γ < m) hmS
  -- The model `μ` has all its means equal to `m`, and `λ j` moves the arm `j` to `ℓ`.
  set μ : α → ℝ := fun _ ↦ m
  set lam : α → α → ℝ := fun j ↦ Function.update μ j ℓ
  have hμS : μ ∈ S := hmS
  have hlam_self (j : α) : lam j j = ℓ := by simp [lam]
  have hlam_ne (j b : α) (hb : b ≠ j) : lam j b = m := by simp [lam, μ, hb]
  have hlamS (j : α) : lam j ∈ S := fun b ↦ by
    by_cases hb : b = j
    · subst hb
      rw [hlam_self]
      exact hℓS b
    · rw [hlam_ne j b hb]
      exact hmS b
  have hμM : μ ∈ task.M := (hMt μ).2 ⟨Or.inr fun _ ↦ hm, hμS⟩
  have hlamM (j : α) : lam j ∈ task.M :=
    (hMt (lam j)).2 ⟨Or.inl ⟨j, by rw [hlam_self]; exact hℓ'⟩, hlamS j⟩
  have hcorr_μ : task.correct μ = {false} := by
    rw [IdentTask.correct_restrict, correct_minThresholdTask_eq_singleton, id_eq,
      decide_eq_false (not_exists.2 fun a ha ↦ lt_asymm ha hm)]
  have hcorr_lam (j : α) : task.correct (lam j) = {true} := by
    rw [IdentTask.correct_restrict, correct_minThresholdTask_eq_singleton, id_eq,
      decide_eq_true ⟨j, by rw [hlam_self]; exact hℓ'⟩]
  have hνeq (j b : α) (hb : b ≠ j) : task.ν (lam j) b = task.ν μ b := by
    rw [hνt, hν (lam j) b (hlamS j b), hν μ b (hμS b), hlam_ne j b hb]
  have hdm (j : α) : 0 < (ρ j).expFamilyDiv id m ℓ :=
    Measure.expFamilyDiv_pos (hmS j) (hℓS j) (hℓ'.trans hm).ne'
  have hKL (j : α) : klDiv (task.ν μ j) (task.ν (lam j) j) =
      ENNReal.ofReal ((ρ j).expFamilyDiv id m ℓ) := by
    rw [hνt, hν μ j (hμS j), hν (lam j) j (hlamS j j), hlam_self]
    exact Measure.klDiv_expFamily_natParam (hmS j) (hℓS j)
  -- `H^{sp}(λ j)` is at most `KL_j(γ, ℓ)⁻¹`, and positive: `μ` is an alternative to `λ j`.
  have hH_le (j : α) : task.staticDifficulty (lam j) ≤
      (ENNReal.ofReal ((ρ j).expFamilyDiv id γ ℓ))⁻¹ := by
    have h := staticDifficulty_minThresholdTask_le ν hν hγ (hlamS j) (j := j)
      (by rw [hlam_self]; exact hℓ')
    rwa [hlam_self] at h
  have hμalt (j : α) : μ ∈ task.alternatives (lam j) := by
    rw [task.alternatives_eq_alt (hcorr_lam j), IdentTask.alt_restrict]
    exact ⟨(mem_alt_minThresholdTask_true_iff ν id).2 fun _ ↦ hm, hμS⟩
  have hV_le (j : α) :
      ⨆ w ∈ simplex α, ⨅ μ' ∈ task.alternatives (lam j), task.cost w μ' (lam j) ≤
        ENNReal.ofReal ((ρ j).expFamilyDiv id m ℓ) := by
    refine iSup₂_le fun w hw ↦ (iInf₂_le μ (hμalt j)).trans ?_
    rw [IdentTask.cost_def, Finset.sum_eq_single j
      (fun b _ hb ↦ by rw [hνeq j b hb, klDiv_self, mul_zero]) (by simp), hKL j]
    calc ENNReal.ofReal (w j) * ENNReal.ofReal ((ρ j).expFamilyDiv id m ℓ)
        ≤ 1 * ENNReal.ofReal ((ρ j).expFamilyDiv id m ℓ) := by
          gcongr
          exact ENNReal.ofReal_le_one.2 ((simplex_subset_Icc hw).2 j)
      _ = _ := one_mul _
  by_cases hp : Tendsto (task.errorProb 𝒜 μ) atTop (𝓝 0)
  swap
  · -- If the probability of error at `μ` does not tend to `0`, the ratio at `μ` is infinite:
    -- `H^{sp}(μ)` is finite, as the alternatives to `μ` cost at least `min_b KL_b(γ, m) / K`
    -- with the uniform allocation.
    have hfin : task.staticDifficulty μ ≠ ∞ := by
      rw [IdentTask.staticDifficulty, ENNReal.inv_ne_top]
      have : Nonempty α := nonempty_of_isProbabilityMeasure ((𝒜 0).alg.policyZero ())
      obtain ⟨b₀, hb₀⟩ := exists_eq_ciInf_of_finite (f := fun b ↦ (ρ b).expFamilyRate id γ m)
      have hpos : 0 < ENNReal.ofReal (Fintype.card α : ℝ)⁻¹ * (ρ b₀).expFamilyRate id γ m := by
        rw [Measure.expFamilyRate_eq_ofReal_expFamilyDiv (hγ b₀) (hmS b₀)]
        exact ENNReal.mul_pos (ENNReal.ofReal_pos.2 (by positivity)).ne'
          (ENNReal.ofReal_pos.2 (Measure.expFamilyDiv_pos (hγ b₀) (hmS b₀) hm.ne)).ne'
      refine (lt_of_lt_of_le hpos ?_).ne'
      refine le_iSup₂_of_le _ (uniform_mem_simplex (α := α)) (le_iInf₂ fun μ' hμ' ↦ ?_)
      rw [task.alternatives_eq_alt hcorr_μ, IdentTask.alt_restrict] at hμ'
      obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := (mem_alt_minThresholdTask_false_iff ν id).1 hμ'.1
      have hμ'S : μ' ∈ S := hμ'.2
      rw [IdentTask.cost_def]
      refine le_trans ?_ (Finset.single_le_sum (f := fun b ↦ ENNReal.ofReal
        (Fintype.card α : ℝ)⁻¹ * klDiv (task.ν μ' b) (task.ν μ b)) (fun b _ ↦ zero_le)
        (Finset.mem_univ a))
      gcongr
      calc (ρ b₀).expFamilyRate id γ m = ⨅ b, (ρ b).expFamilyRate id γ m := hb₀
        _ ≤ (ρ a).expFamilyRate id γ m := iInf_le _ a
        _ ≤ (ρ a).expFamilyRate id (μ' a) m :=
          Measure.antitoneOn_expFamilyRate_left (hmS a) (Set.mem_Iic.2 (ha.le.trans hm.le))
            (Set.mem_Iic.2 hm.le) ha.le
        _ = klDiv (task.ν μ' a) (task.ν μ a) := by
          rw [hνt, hν μ' a (hμ'S a), hν μ a (hμS a),
            Measure.klDiv_expFamily_natParam (hμ'S a) (hμS a),
            Measure.expFamilyRate_eq_ofReal_expFamilyDiv (hμ'S a) (hμS a)]
    refine le_trans le_top (le_of_eq ?_)
    rw [eq_comm, eq_top_iff, ← task.asymptoticRatio_eq_top hfin hp]
    exact le_iSup₂ (f := fun θ (_ : θ ∈ task.M) ↦ task.asymptoticRatio _ 𝒜 θ) μ hμM
  -- Corollary 4 at `μ` with the alternatives `λ j`.
  have hcor := sum_inv_le_iSup_asymptoticRatio task task.staticDifficulty h𝒜 hp Finset.univ lam
    (fun j _ ↦ by
      rw [hcorr_μ, hcorr_lam j]
      exact Set.disjoint_singleton.2 Bool.false_ne_true)
    (fun j _ b hb ↦ hνeq j b hb)
    (fun j _ ↦ by
      rw [IdentTask.staticDifficulty, ENNReal.inv_ne_zero]
      exact ne_top_of_le_ne_top ENNReal.ofReal_ne_top (hV_le j))
    (fun j _ ↦ ne_top_of_le_ne_top (ENNReal.inv_ne_top.2 (ENNReal.ofReal_pos.2 (hdγ j)).ne')
      (hH_le j))
  calc ENNReal.ofReal (∑ b, (ρ b).expFamilyDiv id γ ℓ / (ρ b).expFamilyDiv id m ℓ)
      = ∑ j, ENNReal.ofReal ((ρ j).expFamilyDiv id γ ℓ / (ρ j).expFamilyDiv id m ℓ) :=
        ENNReal.ofReal_sum_of_nonneg fun j _ ↦ (div_pos (hdγ j) (hdm j)).le
    _ ≤ ∑ j, (task.staticDifficulty (lam j) * klDiv (task.ν μ j) (task.ν (lam j) j))⁻¹ := by
        refine Finset.sum_le_sum fun j _ ↦ ?_
        calc ENNReal.ofReal ((ρ j).expFamilyDiv id γ ℓ / (ρ j).expFamilyDiv id m ℓ)
            = ((ENNReal.ofReal ((ρ j).expFamilyDiv id γ ℓ))⁻¹ *
                ENNReal.ofReal ((ρ j).expFamilyDiv id m ℓ))⁻¹ := by
              rw [ENNReal.mul_inv (Or.inr ENNReal.ofReal_ne_top)
                (Or.inr (ENNReal.ofReal_pos.2 (hdm j)).ne'), inv_inv,
                ENNReal.ofReal_div_of_pos (hdm j), div_eq_mul_inv]
          _ ≤ _ := by
              rw [hKL j]
              exact ENNReal.inv_le_inv.2 (by gcongr; exact hH_le j)
    _ ≤ ⨆ j ∈ Finset.univ, task.asymptoticRatio task.staticDifficulty 𝒜 (lam j) := hcor
    _ ≤ task.maxRatio task.staticDifficulty 𝒜 :=
        iSup₂_le fun j _ ↦ le_iSup₂ (f := fun θ (_ : θ ∈ task.M) ↦
          task.asymptoticRatio task.staticDifficulty 𝒜 θ) (lam j) (hlamM j)

/-- **Positivity has maximal difficulty ratio `K`** [D23, Theorem 6]. Let the arm `a` belong to
the exponential family generated by `ρ a` with the statistic `id`, not almost everywhere
constant, and let the threshold `γ` be a mean of every family.
For the positivity task (minimum threshold at `γ`) on the vectors of means of the families, the
infimum over the fixed-budget algorithm families of the maximal difficulty ratio to the
static-proportions difficulty is `K`, the number of arms.

Uniform sampling, recommending whether some empirical mean is below `γ`, attains it
(`maxRatio_staticDifficulty_minThresholdTask_le`), and no family does better
(`card_le_maxRatio_minThresholdTask`). -/
theorem iInf_maxRatio_minThresholdTask_eq_card (ν : (α → ℝ) → Kernel α ℝ)
    [∀ μ, IsMarkovKernel (ν μ)] {ρ : α → Measure ℝ} (hρ : ∀ a c, ¬ id =ᵐ[ρ a] fun _ ↦ c)
    (hν : ∀ μ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id →
      ν μ a = (ρ a).expFamily id ((ρ a).natParam id (μ a)))
    {γ : ℝ} (hγ : ∀ a, γ ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id) :
    ⨅ (𝒜 : ℕ → IdentAlg Unit α ℝ Bool) (_ : IsFixedBudgetFamily 𝒜),
      ((minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict {μ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}).maxRatio
        ((minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict
          {μ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}).staticDifficulty 𝒜 = Fintype.card α := by
  classical
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (le_iInf₂ fun 𝒜 h𝒜 ↦ card_le_maxRatio_minThresholdTask ν hρ hν hγ h𝒜)
  have hK : (0 : ℝ) < Fintype.card α := by exact_mod_cast Fintype.card_pos
  -- Uniform sampling, recommending whether some empirical mean is below `γ`.
  set rec : (α → ℝ) → Bool := fun x ↦ decide (∃ a, x a < γ)
  have hrec (x : α → ℝ) : rec x = true ↔ ∃ a, x a < γ := decide_eq_true_iff
  have hrecm : Measurable rec := by
    refine measurable_to_bool ?_
    have : rec ⁻¹' {true} = ⋃ a, {x | x a < γ} := by
      ext x
      simp [hrec]
    rw [this]
    exact MeasurableSet.iUnion fun a ↦ measurableSet_lt (measurable_pi_apply a) measurable_const
  obtain ⟨𝒜, h𝒜⟩ := ((minThresholdTask ν id γ).restrict
    {μ | ∀ a, μ a ∈ (ρ a).expFamilyMeans id}).exists_isStaticProportions hrecm
    (w := fun _ ↦ 1 / (Fintype.card α : ℝ)) (fun _ ↦ by positivity)
    (by rw [Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ, nsmul_eq_mul]; field_simp)
  refine (iInf₂_le 𝒜 fun T ↦ (h𝒜.2.2 T).1).trans
    ((maxRatio_staticDifficulty_minThresholdTask_le ν hρ hν hγ hrec h𝒜).trans_eq ?_)
  rw [iInf_const, ENNReal.ofReal_div_of_pos hK, ENNReal.ofReal_one, ENNReal.ofReal_natCast,
    ENNReal.inv_div (Or.inl (ENNReal.natCast_ne_top _)) (Or.inl (by simp)), div_one]

end Degenne2023Existence
